WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.151
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level two.

2
00:00:06.451 --> 00:00:09.791
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.091 --> 00:00:17.480
Unit eighteen: Sustainable Business. Today you will express obligation with be required to, be obliged to and be bound to.

4
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.514
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:24.700
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.132
Corporate responsibility.

7
00:00:28.117 --> 00:00:32.833
Corporate responsibility means a company's duty to act ethically toward people and nature.

8
00:00:33.417 --> 00:00:37.204
Corporate responsibility is now part of every annual report.

9
00:00:37.817 --> 00:00:41.282
Your turn. Say: Corporate responsibility.

10
00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:45.866
Corporate responsibility.

11
00:00:46.617 --> 00:00:47.943
Carbon footprint.

12
00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:53.063
Carbon footprint means the amount of carbon dioxide produced by an activity.

13
00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:56.335
The factory cut its carbon footprint by a third.

14
00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.974
Your turn. Say: Carbon footprint.

15
00:01:02.833 --> 00:01:04.252
Carbon footprint.

16
00:01:05.017 --> 00:01:06.296
Ethical sourcing.

17
00:01:07.283 --> 00:01:11.802
Ethical sourcing means buying materials in ways that respect people and the environment.

18
00:01:12.417 --> 00:01:15.426
Ethical sourcing guarantees fair pay for farmers.

19
00:01:16.017 --> 00:01:19.250
Your turn. Say: Ethical sourcing.

20
00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.507
Ethical sourcing.

21
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.437
Green initiative.

22
00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:30.458
Green initiative means a project designed to protect the environment.

23
00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:33.909
The green initiative planted ten thousand trees.

24
00:01:34.517 --> 00:01:37.494
Your turn. Say: Green initiative.

25
00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.601
Green initiative.

26
00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:44.141
Sustainable supply chain.

27
00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:50.679
Sustainable supply chain means a chain of production that causes little harm to nature.

28
00:01:51.283 --> 00:01:54.072
A sustainable supply chain reduces waste.

29
00:01:54.683 --> 00:01:58.218
Your turn. Say: Sustainable supply chain.

30
00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:03.020
Sustainable supply chain.

31
00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:05.713
Environmental impact.

32
00:02:06.717 --> 00:02:10.922
Environmental impact means the effect an activity has on nature.

33
00:02:11.517 --> 00:02:15.258
The report measured the environmental impact of the mine.

34
00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:19.106
Your turn. Say: Environmental impact.

35
00:02:21.967 --> 00:02:24.477
Environmental impact.

36
00:02:25.217 --> 00:02:26.427
Stakeholder value.

37
00:02:27.417 --> 00:02:32.435
Stakeholder value means benefit for everyone affected by a company, not only owners.

38
00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:35.944
Stakeholder value includes workers and neighbours.

39
00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:39.284
Your turn. Say: Stakeholder value.

40
00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.506
Stakeholder value.

41
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:45.994
Long-term sustainability.

42
00:02:46.983 --> 00:02:52.489
Long-term sustainability means the ability of a business to continue without exhausting resources.

43
00:02:53.083 --> 00:02:56.523
Long-term sustainability protects future profits.

44
00:02:57.117 --> 00:03:00.767
Your turn. Say: Long-term sustainability.

45
00:03:03.633 --> 00:03:06.364
Long-term sustainability.

46
00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:11.061
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:03:11.917 --> 00:03:19.213
Visal, a news analysis says 'Large firms may soon be required to report their carbon footprint.' What does 'be required to' show?

48
00:03:20.317 --> 00:03:29.668
A legal or formal obligation. Be required to, be obliged to and be bound by all describe duties that come from a rule.

49
00:03:30.783 --> 00:03:32.318
Is it different from must?

50
00:03:33.417 --> 00:03:46.834
Must is direct. The passive forms sound more formal and let us omit the person who makes the rule: 'Companies are obliged to disclose their environmental impact.'

51
00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:49.276
And 'be bound to'?

52
00:03:50.383 --> 00:03:58.983
Be bound to + verb means 'certain to'. 'Weak corporate responsibility is bound to damage long-term sustainability.'

53
00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:01.854
Part three: grammar.

54
00:04:02.717 --> 00:04:07.793
Grammar focus: Obligation: be required to and be obliged to and be bound to.

55
00:04:08.093 --> 00:04:09.291
Look at the pattern.

56
00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:13.527
Large firms may be required to report their carbon footprint.

57
00:04:14.417 --> 00:04:18.494
Companies are obliged to disclose their environmental impact.

58
00:04:19.383 --> 00:04:22.242
Weak responsibility is bound to damage the brand.

59
00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:30.708
Be required/obliged to + base verb states a duty. Be bound to + base verb means 'certain to'. Do not add 'must' as well.

60
00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:35.902
Be careful! Don't say: Firms must be required report data.

61
00:04:37.867 --> 00:04:40.783
Say: Firms may be required to report data.

62
00:04:41.083 --> 00:04:43.536
Use be required + to + verb.

63
00:04:44.333 --> 00:04:47.171
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:47.967 --> 00:04:49.362
Business and the Planet.

65
00:04:49.662 --> 00:04:53.891
Companies are under growing pressure to show corporate responsibility.

66
00:04:54.900 --> 00:05:01.811
Large firms may soon be required to report their carbon footprint and the environmental impact of each supply chain.

67
00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:07.470
Ethical sourcing and green initiatives are bound to attract customers who care about nature.

68
00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:12.498
A sustainable supply chain protects stakeholder value as well as profit.

69
00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:17.740
Long-term sustainability is therefore both a duty and an opportunity.

70
00:05:18.833 --> 00:05:22.928
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:23.783 --> 00:05:27.037
Large firms may blank required to report their footprint.

72
00:05:27.337 --> 00:05:30.352
A, be. B, being. C, to be.

73
00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.772
The answer is A: be.

74
00:05:36.917 --> 00:05:40.832
Buying materials in ways that respect people and nature is blank sourcing.

75
00:05:41.132 --> 00:05:44.774
A, ethical. B, carbon. C, green.

76
00:05:48.333 --> 00:05:50.182
The answer is A: ethical.

77
00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:54.942
The effect an activity has on nature is its blank impact.

78
00:05:55.242 --> 00:05:59.383
A, market. B, environmental. C, stakeholder.

79
00:06:02.933 --> 00:06:05.235
The answer is B: environmental.

80
00:06:06.383 --> 00:06:08.127
Which phrase means 'certain to'?

81
00:06:08.427 --> 00:06:12.290
A, is bound to. B, is allowed to. C, is asked to.

82
00:06:15.833 --> 00:06:18.007
The answer is A: is bound to.

83
00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:23.402
According to the reading, sustainability is both a duty and an…

84
00:06:23.702 --> 00:06:26.961
A, opportunity. B, accident. C, advert.

85
00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:32.790
The answer is A: opportunity.

86
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.001
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:42.055
Should companies be required by law to reduce their environmental impact?

88
00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.246
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:52.546 --> 00:07:20.223
I believe companies should be required by law to reduce their environmental impact, because voluntary action is often too slow and uneven. A legal duty creates fair competition, since every firm follows the same rule. On the other hand, regulation should be realistic, with enough time and support for small businesses. Overall, I think clear laws would protect everyone's future.

90
00:07:20.523 --> 00:07:22.197
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:23.083 --> 00:07:29.718
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and obligation: be required to and be obliged to and be bound to.

92
00:07:30.018 --> 00:07:36.455
Today's value is environmental responsibility. Small green actions at home help the whole planet.

93
00:07:36.755 --> 00:07:39.222
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

94
00:07:39.522 --> 00:07:42.070
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

